{
  "text": "On the authority of Abu Abdur Rahman Abdullah, the son of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased of them both, who said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, may the blessings and peace of Allah be upon him, say, Islam has been built on five pillars, testifying that there is no God but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, performing the prayers, paying the zakat, making the pilgrimage to the house, and fasting in Ramadan. It was related by al-Bukhari and Muslim.",
